## Final Judgement
Based on the recorded evidence, the key finding is that Hunter Biden served as Chairman of the board for **World Food Program USA**, which is a separate U.S.-based nonprofit organization that supports the United Nations World Food Programme (WFP). The UN WFP is the entity that won the 2020 Nobel Peace Prize. The evidence clearly distinguishes between these two organizations and shows no record of Hunter Biden holding a chairman or senior leadership role within the UN WFP itself.

The information is sufficient to reach a conclusion. The claim conflates the two distinct entities, presenting a technically true fact (his chairmanship of the U.S. affiliate) in a way that misleads by implying he chaired the Nobel Prize-winning UN organization. This omission of crucial context creates a significantly different impression.

Therefore, the claim is technically true but misleading due to the exclusion of important context. The appropriate decision is `cherry-picking`.

### Verdict: CHERRY_PICKING

### Justification
The fact-check reveals that Hunter Biden served as Chairman of the board for **World Food Program USA**, a U.S.-based nonprofit that supports the UN's World Food Programme (WFP), but he did not hold a leadership role within the UN WFP itself, which is the organization that won the [2020 Nobel Peace Prize](https://www.nbcnews.com/news/world/world-food-program-wins-2020-nobel-peace-prize-n1242678). The claim is therefore deemed misleading for omitting this critical distinction between the two separate entities, a classic case of cherry-picking.